      "message": "fix(sim): refuse a feed plunge deeper than one stepdown below the uncut floor\n\nThe plunge depth law (crates/sim/src/verify/plunge_depth.rs) judges each non-Rapid axial descent. It samples the full tool disc and reads rest.surface_before, so it names a feed plunge that goes deeper than one stepdown below the floor that the levels above left under the disc.\n\nThe law is gated by VerifyContext::plunge_stepdown. None keeps the law silent. The app selector in cutting_rows gives the operation's stated stepdown; a Face with no stepdown passes None.\n\nThe finding is an advisory PlungeTooDeep warning: it names the move, the depth and the limit. It does not block the post until issue #3678 lands.\n\nTests: the sim binary plunge_depth pins the #3678 numbers; the app test plunge_depth_tab names the three dives in the contour-tabs catalog case.\n\nFixes #3679",
