      "message": "fix(sim): acquit the plunge law on prior-cut material and keep it within its stepdown slack\n\nThe first law read the whole column below this op's own rest floor, and\nover-convicted six pre-existing app suites. Two readings were wrong.\n\nThe bite: a plunge move takes only the material between its own start\nand its end. The bite's floor is the lesser of the move's start and\nthe rest surface. A dive from air keeps the old reading whole, and a\nstart the rest cannot read falls back to the move's own start, an\nupper bound the bite cannot pass. The slot entry behind a rapid that\nbroke the raw top (vertical_rapid_stock) and the 18 trochoidal\nmicrolift plunges (carried_stock_entry) acquit.\n\nThe prior: a dive into material that a program-ahead operation\nalready cut reads the prior surface, the same third term of the min\nthat acquit_by_prior gives a rapid (acquit_plunge_by_prior, wired\nbeside it in generate.rs). The faced-block dives\n(vertical_rapid_stock, clearance_in_stock, top_stock) and the carried\ncontour plunge (carried_stock_entry, 10.0 faced against a 10.5 raw\ntop) acquit.\n\nThe slack stays the established z_tol alone: the 0.5 mm overage of\nthe trochoid pecks was a floor error and a bite error, not a\ntolerance error. Each of the six resolutions is recorded in\ndocs/decisions/3679-plunge-depth-law.md. The crescent case of the\nissue is unchanged - its dive starts in air, and no prior program cut\nthe sheet at the tab window (plunge_depth sim binary,\nplunge_depth_tab).\n\nFixes #3679",
